nvrm-info on a real board, 2026-11-22 (Track #2362)
====================================================

Real, captured by tests/libnvrm/boot_nvrm_info.sh in a test boot of amp001 (an
RTX 5060 Ti, device unit 1, a BMC display on unit 0).  Never edited:

  nvrm-info.json   nvrm-info --json of that boot (library before the fixes:
                   no compute capability, no versions object,
                   running_rm_version unavailable)
  sysctl.txt       hw.nvidia.version, altra_device_wc_active, hw.nvidia.gpus.*
                   (no dev.nvidia.*, no hw.nvidia.version_*: not yet captured)
  pciconf.txt      pciconf -lvb
  results.txt      the four FAIL rows this capture produced

Derived, written by make-after.py (python3 -I make-after.py [DIR]) from the
real files; only the fields the fixed code adds, with the values the fixed code
gives for this boot's raw values:

  nvrm-info.after.json  schema_minor 2; gpu.rm_sm_version 2564 (0x0A04);
                        gpu.compute_capability_major/minor 12/0 (derived);
                        top-level versions with driver (source os) and
                        built_for (derived) only; running_rm_version available
                        "580.178.04" (source os).  Not complete against the
                        schema: the device versions group and the other
                        versions members are not added, no comparison reads them.
  sysctl.after.txt      the real sysctl.txt plus hw.nvidia.version_string,
                        _major, _minor, _patch, _suffix, _available and
                        dev.nvidia.1.uuid, .pci_bus_id (000d:01:00.0) and
                        .%location, in the output form of sysctl(8).

tests/libnvrm/boot_fixture_test.sh runs boot_compare.py on the original (the
SM, uuid, running-version and versions rows must FAIL) and on the derived
fixture (every row must PASS), and on mutations of the derived one.
